{"h": {"measure": "P", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 123, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 2 removed, node 1 can reach the output only through edge 4, so improving edge 0 matters less and does nothing when edge 4 is also absent."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 5 is none, node 2 has no path to the output, so a conv on edge 0->2 cannot affect the cell's output."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the direct 0->3 edge, removing edge 5 cuts one of very few remaining input-output paths and can disconnect the cell, so the drop is much larger."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual where there was none gives a large gain from better gradient flow, while replacing an existing conv or pool with skip is roughly neutral or harmful."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv with parameter-free pooling loses capacity, whereas replacing a skip with pooling changes little."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping a conv for pooling on an edge feeding the output removes learnable capacity, which a skip-to-pool swap does not."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Edge 0 is the first stage of the deepest path, and losing its conv hurts more than replacing a skip there."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 0 is none, node 1 carries zeros, so a conv on edge 1->3 processes nothing useful."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 absent, removing edge 3 leaves only edge 4 feeding the output, starving the cell of paths and badly hurting accuracy."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If node 1 is dead because edge 0 is none, a conv on edge 1->2 receives zero input and adds nothing."}], "tok": 30081, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [1, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [1, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [1, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [1, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["